[stderr] +
[stderr] +The catalogue contains stable, unique IDs in three namespaces: `FDN-01` to
[stderr] +`FDN-09`, `FEX-01` to `FEX-14`, and `QOR-01` to `QOR-08`. Their authoring
[stderr] +sequence is foundation first, feature/experience next, and quality/release
[stderr] +evidence throughout and at the release gate. `05-delivery-map.md` supplies the
[stderr] +implementation sequence (`DM-01` to `DM-20`) and closure for the planned code
[stderr] +boundaries; its numbered order must not be treated as permission to bypass a
[stderr] +listed approval gate.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +One metadata gap was corrected in this audit: FEX-09 had browser-facing
[stderr] +feedback assertions but delegated them to three other feature specs. That
[stderr] +violated the unique browser-spec ownership convention in 07. FEX-09 now owns
[stderr] +`supervisor/browser/tests/changes/fex-09-feedback.spec.*`; no implementation
[stderr] +spec exists yet because this repository is still planning-only.
